cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ThreadBench, please cite the paper below."
title: "ThreadBench"
abstract: >-
  ThreadBench is a benchmark for measuring realism in LLM-based social
  simulation of Reddit discussions. It contains 9,817 real Reddit threads
  across 8 domains and 116 reported subdomains, and compares generated and
  held-out real threads with 12 metrics in four families (Uniformity,
  Expression, Tone, Interaction) using two-sided Mann-Whitney U and
  Kolmogorov-Smirnov tests. This repository contains the earlier MiroBench
  implementation and five-domain data release.
